# Game Asset Storage Addendum (.gitattributes)
#
# Append these lines to the repository root .gitattributes AFTER the starter's
# core lines, because later rules win in .gitattributes.
#
# Why this matters: the starter sets `* text=auto eol=lf` for all repositories.
# Git cannot always infer that game asset files are binary, and a text-mode
# checkout corrupts them. Every large-file or binary rule must therefore end in
# `-text` so the core normalization rule stops applying.
#
# This file is an example addendum. It is NOT active in this repository.
# Copy the lines you need into your own .gitattributes and delete the rest.

# --- Option A: large-file storage for authoring masters (directory-scoped) ---
# Prefer directory scope over extension scope. Tracking every *.png as a large
# file is usually a mistake: runtime images are small, and metered large-file
# storage is consumed again on every CI clone.
#
# app/game/assets/masters/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# art/**                     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- Option B: no large-file storage, explicit binary markers only ---
# Use this when masters live outside the repository, or all assets are small.
# Without these lines Git usually detects binary content correctly, but the
# explicit marker removes the guesswork for unusual formats.
#
# app/game/assets/masters/** binary
# art/**                     binary

# --- Authored data: keep as reviewable text ---
# Tiled maps, atlas descriptors, and level data are JSON and should diff well.
# Verify the current extension used by your tool version before relying on it.
*.tmj   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# --- Unity YAML assets: use the engine's merge tool, not plain text ---
# Only relevant if the repo also contains Unity projects. The merge driver must
# be registered in .git/config or the merge silently falls back to text.
# *.unity   merge=unityyamlmerge eol=lf
# *.prefab  merge=unityyamlmerge eol=lf

# --- Reminder ---
# After changing this file, renormalize once:
#   git add --renormalize .
# Then verify attribute resolution for a representative asset path:
#   git check-attr text eol filter -- app/game/assets/masters/example.aseprite
